Tue Nov 03 01:23:50 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Parse a successful update check from zypper's stdout only. stderr
  is kept for the failure text, so a warning does not make the XML
  parser reject the update list.
- After cancel, send SIGTERM and wait ten seconds before SIGKILL, so
  transactional-update can discard the snapshot.
- Do not restart packagekitd from %post while TRANSACTIONAL_UPDATE
  is set. That restart hits the daemon which is running the update.
- Show an ERROR: line from snapper or the snapshot tools. Exit 4
  without a dependency sentence is a transaction error.
- Release 10. The repository already has 0.1.0-9.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 01:02:33 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- When the package transaction fails, show the conflict. zypper writes
  that on stderr. The stdout tail was the download cache, "exit status
  8", and "Discarding snapshot".
- Say, in plain language, when two packages own one file or a dependency
  cannot be satisfied. transactional-update exits 1 for every zypper
  failure, so the real code is taken from "failed with exit code".
  A failure that gives no reason still says nothing was changed.
- Keep the two command streams apart until the command exits, then
  append stderr. A progress line no longer lands in the middle of a
  conflict line.
- Release 9.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 00:33:19 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- When a repository file returns HTTP 404, name the missing packages.
  Discover keeps the tail of a long error, which was the snapshot
  cleanup, so a rebuild in progress looked like a silent failure.
- Release 8. The repository already has 0.1.0-7.1.

